# Multi-Tenant Implementation Plan (Revised)

## Problem & Context

SCMS has **two frontend apps**:
- **`:4200`** — Owner/master SCMS application (tenant management, modules, plans, etc.)
- **`:4201`, `:4202`, …** — Tenant-specific clinics

Every API request (except owner routes and `/resolve`) must carry an `x-tenant-code` header. But **tenants don't know their code upfront** — the frontend discovers it at app startup by calling a `/resolve` endpoint with its Origin URL.

---

## High-Level Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant FE as Angular App (e.g. :4201)
    participant API as SCMS Backend
    participant ScmsDB as ScmsDbContext (Tenants table)
    participant Cache as IMemoryCache
    participant EnvVar as Environment Variables

    Note over FE: ngOnInit — app bootstrap
    FE->>API: GET /api/tenant/v1/resolve<br/>Origin: http://localhost:4201
    API->>ScmsDB: Tenants.FirstOrDefault(t => t.DomainUrl == origin && t.IsActive)
    ScmsDB-->>API: Tenant { TenantCode: "clinica", Name: "Clinic A", ... }
    API-->>FE: { tenantCode, name, logoUrl }
    Note over FE: Store tenantCode in memory/service

    FE->>API: GET /api/tenant/v1/departments<br/>x-tenant-code: clinica
    API->>API: TenantResolverMiddleware
    API->>Cache: tenantctx::CLINICA?
    alt Cache miss
        API->>EnvVar: SCMS_CLINICA_SHARED_CONNECTION
        EnvVar-->>API: "Host=localhost;..."
        API->>ScmsDB: Tenants.Any(code == "clinica" && IsActive)
        ScmsDB-->>API: true
        API->>Cache: Set(tenantctx::CLINICA, state)
    end
    Note over API: ITenantContext populated
    API->>API: TenantDbContext uses ConnectionString
    API-->>FE: 200 { departments... }
