## Part 1 — Tenant Resolution (`/resolve` Endpoint)

### What it does

The Angular tenant app calls `GET /api/tenant/v1/resolve` on startup (`ngOnInit`). The API reads the `Origin` header (or `Referer` fallback), matches it against the `DomainUrl` column in the `Tenants` table, and returns the tenant's public details.

> [!NOTE]
> The `/resolve` endpoint is **unauthenticated** and **does not require `x-tenant-code`** — it's the endpoint that _provides_ the tenant code.

### How the frontend uses it

```typescript
// Angular — AppComponent or APP_INITIALIZER
ngOnInit() {
  this.http.get('/api/tenant/v1/resolve').subscribe(res => {
    this.tenantService.setCode(res.data.tenantCode);
    // All subsequent HTTP calls add: x-tenant-code: <tenantCode>
  });
}
```

