## Part 3 — Naming Convention & Validation

### Tenant Code → Environment Variable Mapping

| Tenant Code | Env Var Name |
|---|---|
| `clinica` | `SCMS_CLINICA_SHARED_CONNECTION` |
| `clinic-b` | `SCMS_CLINIC_B_SHARED_CONNECTION` |
| `vktech` | `SCMS_VKTECH_SHARED_CONNECTION` |

**Rule**: `code.ToUpperInvariant().Replace("-", "_")` → `SCMS_{result}_SHARED_CONNECTION`

### Validation

The existing DB constraint (`ck_tenant_code_alnum_hyphen`) already enforces:
- Alphanumeric + hyphens only
- No leading/trailing hyphens
- No double hyphens

We add **application-level validation** in `TenantContext.ResolveAsync`:

```csharp
private static readonly Regex ValidTenantCode = new(
    @"^(?!-)(?!.*--)[A-Za-z0-9-]+(?<!-)$",
    RegexOptions.Compiled);

// in ResolveAsync:
if (!ValidTenantCode.IsMatch(rawCode))
    throw new BadRequestException($"Invalid tenant code format: '{rawCode}'");
```

This matches the DB constraint exactly, so invalid codes are rejected before any env-var/DB lookup.

